  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In first step nitration occurs by mixture of concentrated nitric acid and concentrated sulphuric acid. From this step nitrobenzene (A) is produced.</p><p>In next step chlorination of nitrobenzene occurs, nitro group is meta directing which orients the incoming electrophile at meta position which results in formation of compound (B).</p><p>In last step, reduction occurs and nitro group is converted into amino group and produces compound (C).</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ff05fc6c-a183-42e6-9083-816b118a6ea4-04374754-4d47-4f50-b1f0-e539aa4d2cd6-image.png\" style=\"width: 943px; height: 124px;\" /></p>",
